Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `posts_questions.creation_date`: filter to the 2022 calendar year and extract months for grouping.  
• `posts_questions.tags`: detect whether the question contains the tag `<python>` (tags are stored as a single string with angle‑bracket–delimited tags, e.g. `<python><pandas>`).  
• `posts_questions.id`: count distinct questions (acts as the primary key).  

Main conditions you will need  
• `EXTRACT(YEAR  FROM creation_date) = 2022` – keep only 2022 questions.  
• `tags LIKE '%<python>%'` – identify questions that carry the python tag.  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL snippets.  
(Replace nothing – the identifiers are already fully‑qualified.)  
All queries include back‑ticked identifiers and LIMIT 20 as requested.

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at any 20 questions posted in 2022
SELECT id, creation_date, tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample 20  questions that carry the <python> tag in 2022
SELECT id, creation_date, tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
  AND tags LIKE '%<python>%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct tag strings (trimmed to 20 rows) that include python in 2022
SELECT DISTINCT tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
  AND tags LIKE '%<python>%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Total number of questions per month in 2022 (preview 20 rows)
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM creation_date) AS month_num,
  COUNT(DISTINCT id)              AS total_questions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Number of python‑tagged questions per month in 2022 (preview 20 rows)
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM creation_date) AS month_num,
  COUNT(DISTINCT id)              AS python_questions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
  AND tags LIKE '%<python>%'
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Combine the two previous aggregations with a JOIN (top 20 rows)
WITH total AS (
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM creation_date) AS month_num,
         COUNT(DISTINCT id) AS total_q
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
  GROUP BY month_num
),
py AS (
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM creation_date) AS month_num,
         COUNT(DISTINCT id) AS py_q
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
    AND tags LIKE '%<python>%'
  GROUP BY month_num
)
SELECT
  t.month_num,
  py.py_q,
  t.total_q
FROM total t
LEFT JOIN py USING (month_num)
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Use conditional aggregation instead of a join (top 20 rows)
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM creation_date) AS month_num,
  COUNT(*)                                   AS total_q,
  COUNTIF(tags LIKE '%<python>%')            AS py_q
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but also show the proportion (as a decimal) (top 20)
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM creation_date)               AS month_num,
  COUNT(*)                                        AS total_q,
  COUNTIF(tags LIKE '%<python>%')                 AS py_q,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(tags LIKE '%<python>%'), COUNT(*)) AS proportion_py
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Return calendar month name instead of number (top 20)
SELECT
  FORMAT_DATE('%Y-%m', DATE_TRUNC(DATE(creation_date), MONTH)) AS month,
  COUNT(*)                                        AS total_q,
  COUNTIF(tags LIKE '%<python>%')                 AS py_q,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(tags LIKE '%<python>%'), COUNT(*)) AS proportion_py
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: monthly proportion of questions tagged with python in 2022
-- (12 rows expected, one per month, still under the 20‑row limit)
SELECT
  FORMAT_DATE('%Y-%m', DATE_TRUNC(DATE(creation_date), MONTH)) AS month,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(tags LIKE '%<python>%'), COUNT(*))        AS proportion_python
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM creation_date) = 2022
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```
